{{!--
    An admonition written in a doc comment: `@note`, `@warning`, `@tip`,
    `@important`, `@caution`.

    Without this, the Markdown generator falls back to the HTML generator's
    partial, which emits a kind-less `<div class="admonition">` titled by an
    `<h4>`. Material for MkDocs colors and captions an admonition from the kind
    class and an `admonition-title`, so that form renders as an unstyled box
    and looks nothing like the admonitions the generator itself produces. Keep
    this in step with `markup/admonition.md.hbs`, which handles those.

    The body arrives as block content that already carries its own `<p>` tags,
    so it is not wrapped again: a `@note` may hold a list.
--}}

<div class="admonition {{admonish}}" markdown="0"><p class="admonition-title">{{titlecase admonish}}</p>
{{> doc/block-container ~}}
</div>

